# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the harness
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/tsan.supp ./build-tsan/harness ...
#
# macOS recycles a finished detached thread's pthread block, where errno
# lives, for the next new thread, and TSan does not reset that range when
# the new thread starts, so errno accesses in two unrelated threads look
# like a race. os_signal saves and restores errno (it runs in signal
# handlers too) and os_wait reads it after failed calls, so they are the
# ones reported. They touch nothing else shared but the event's
# descriptors, which never change after os_eventinit.
race:os_signal
race:os_wait
